{
  "index_test": "whole-animal-in-vivo",
  "index_test_evidence": "Study selection Animal studies for interventions with unambiguous evidence of a treatment effect (benefit or harm) in clinical trials: head injury, antifibrinolytics in haemorrhage, thrombolysis in acute ischaemic stroke, tirilazad in acute ischaemic stroke, antenatal corticosteroids to prevent neonatal respiratory distress syndrome, and bisphosphonates to treat osteoporosis. Review methods Data were extracted on study design, allocation concealment, number of randomised animals, type of model, intervention, and outcome.",
  "decision": "include",
  "reason": "The study systematically reviews animal experiments and compares their results to clinical trials for several intervention-indication pairs, reporting quantitative measures of agreement (e.g., odds ratios, effect sizes) and discussing concordance/discordance."
}
